<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="sparc:BE:32:default:default">
<!--
    GH-6990: "Sparc 32 defaulting to returning undefined8 for void"
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/6990

    Source:   main is a void no-op function:
                  save %sp,-0xb8,%sp ; nop ; restore ; retl ; nop
              (real `main` @ 0x32148 in binaries/6990/SPARC_GCC_O0_pcodtest.txt,
               SPARC32 BE, GCC -O0; bytes verbatim below)

    The bug:  xunknown8 main(xunknown4 param_1,xunknown4 param_2)
              { return CONCAT44(param_2,param_1); }

    Root cause: SparcV9_32.cspec <output> joins o0:o1 via
    <rule><datatype name="any" maxsize="8"/><join storage="general"/></rule>.
    On-the-fly return recovery (ActionReturnRecovery) marks BOTH o0 and o1
    output trials active because their prologue values pass through the
    save/restore window to the RETURN: realistic, but passive, ancestry.
    buildReturnOutput then emits CONCAT44(o1,o0) as an 8-byte return.

    This is now fixed BY DEFAULT, and on every architecture: kuna_returnuncomputed
    inspects the built pair once heritage has settled and rewrites the RETURN to
    the half that carries a value the function actually computed, dropping the
    passive one.  The same repair is what stops x86-64 SysV rendering
    `undefined16 main(...)` with a phantom `v[8] = <uninitialized stack slot>`.

    `option returnpair single` (P0 assertion, S4 trial finalization) predates it
    and remains the blunt per-function instrument: it refuses ANY multi-register
    join, including a genuine one.  Here the two agree; pass 2 has nothing left
    to drop.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x32148" readonly="true">
9de3bf480100000081e8000081c3e008010000009de3bfa00100000081e80000
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x32148" name="main"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option returnpair single</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH6990 #1: the passive o1 join is dropped in BOTH passes (default already recovers the single-register return)" min="2" max="2">unsigned int main\(unsigned int a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH6990 #2: no CONCAT44 join survives anywhere" min="0" max="0">return CONCAT44\(a1,a0\)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
